      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It is completely understandable to feel desperate when the medo of losing your identity feels so devastating, but the idea that you are already going to suffer a permanent, irreversible decline is a common and dangerous distortion often associated with the very condition you are living through. Dissociation does not mean a slow erasure of your personality; with proper care from a psychiatrist or therapist, your brain can learn to ground you again before anything like that ever happens. Please reach out to a medical professional immediately so we can address these fears with real hope and concrete solutions rather than uncertainty.",
